        "text": "000\nABNT20 KNHC 221126\nTWOAT \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n700 AM EST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nFor the North Atlantic...Caribbean Sea and the Gulf of America:\n\nOffshore of the Southeast U.S. Coast:\nA non-tropical, gale-force low pressure area centered a few hundred \nmiles east of the North Carolina coast is producing disorganized \nshowers and thunderstorms. This low is forecast to move northward \ninto unfavorable environmental conditions, and development into a \ntropical or subtropical system is not expected.\n\nRegardless of the system's status, this large weather system is \nstill expected to produce heavy rains, gusty winds, dangerous surf, \nrip currents, and coastal flooding along portions of the eastern \nU.S. coasts during the next couple of days.  Additional information \non this system, including Gale Warnings, can be found in High Seas \nForecasts issued by the National Weather Service, as well as \nproducts issued by your local National Weather Service forecast \noffice.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...near 0 percent.\n\n&&\nHigh Seas Forecasts issued by the National Weather Service can be \nfound under AWIPS header NFDHSFAT1, WMO header FZNT01 KWBC, and \nonline at ocean.weather.gov/shtml/NFDHSFAT1.php\n\n$$\nForecaster Kelly",
        "tropical_activity": true
      },
